From 11c39dd16f4ca21f3a7666638e422cf1283511ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:28:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 42/51] drm/gma500: capture an sgxfive error state for
 devcoredump

A recovery reset left nothing behind but two lines in the log. Before it
resets, capture a snapshot under the device lock: the time, which
detector fired (BIF fault watchdog, job timeout or debugfs reset), the
suspect job, the guilty context with the pid and command of the process
that opened its file, BIF_INT_STAT and BIF_FAULT, what sgxfive_dump()
shows, and each context's unfinished jobs with their saved firmware
commands, before the guilty ones are failed. It is bounded to eight
contexts and eight commands. Once the reset is done the snapshot goes to
devcoredump on the PCI device and is formatted with drm_coredump_printer
on each read. Capture allocates with GFP_NOWAIT, as it runs in the
drm_sched timeout path, and not at all while a dump is still pending.
sgxfive_dump() now prints the same device snapshot. KUnit covers the
capture, its bounds, the text and reads in pieces.

Assisted-by: LLM
